From 03f38c1acfad2d07bedc9490ee784c5843ca682b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 07:42:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: start-area fleet, spirit rez fallback, paladin/rogue
 rotations (F-219)

- fleet.py: one bot per starting area (9 areas, accounts ZEPF1-9, ports 8100-8108), each with
  its own instance dir under agent-wow-fleet/. `restart [--build]` = stop + reinstall modules +
  FRESH characters + start, so every code change replays all start zones (regressions such as
  the Mechashark one can no longer hide behind a single-zone run). Goblin runs Kezan then the
  Lost Isles as two legs; a leg must PASS before the next starts.
- interact: SpiritHeal RPC (CMSG_SPIRIT_HEALER_ACTIVATE); runner falls back to the nearest spirit
  healer after 2.5 min of failed reclaims (Gobmine's corpse after the Footbomb Uniform death was
  never handed back) - verified: resurrected at 39660.
- runner/supervise/rpc: RPC port from AGENT_WOW_RPC_PORT; supervise.sh takes AW_RUN/AW_BIN/AW_TESTS.
- CLASS_ABILITIES: paladin (aura, blessing, seal, judgement) and rogue (Sinister Strike, Eviscerate).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SQmFdwZBdZ1kNkYTTF4JNJ
